      "content": "that makes sense. but i'm seeing a lot of debate online about how that \"malicious intent\" thing is applied. some people say that if a satire piece relies on harmful stereotypes, it's basically just hate speech disguised as a joke, even if there's no direct threat of violence. do the major platforms actually follow that logic, or do they stick to the strict \"incitement to violence\" rule?",
